meta {
  name: Submit Application
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/master-application
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "city_id": {{city_id}},
    "category_ids": [{{category_id}}],
    "experience_years": 5,
    "about": "Работаю сантехником с 2019 года. Устанавливаю смесители, меняю трубы, устраняю протечки."
  }
}

docs {
  # Submit Master Application

  The "become a master" form. Creates a master profile on this client account
  with status `pending` and puts it in the administrator's review queue. It
  grants nothing by itself — the master endpoints stay closed until the
  administrator approves the profile **and** issues a subscription after taking
  payment in person.

  Name and phone are copied from the client account, so complete the profile
  first (`01_auth` → Complete Registration) or this returns `422`.

  **Fields:**

  | Field              | Rules                                                      |
  |--------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `city_id`          | required, must exist in `cities`                            |
  | `category_ids`     | required, 1..10 ids, **subcategories only** (`parent_id` not null) |
  | `experience_years` | required, integer 0..70                                     |
  | `about`            | optional, up to 1000 chars                                  |

  Root categories are rejected on purpose: they are headings in the catalog,
  not trades. Take the ids from `children[]` in `02_catalog` → List Categories.

  **Response 201:** `MasterApplicationResource` with `status: "pending"`.

  **Re-applying:** allowed only after a rejection — the same row is reused and
  goes back to `pending`, keeping one master profile per account.

  **Errors:**
  - `422` — validation error, root category id, client has no name yet, or
    already applied:
    ```json
    { "message": "Ваша заявка уже на рассмотрении" }
    { "message": "Вы уже являетесь мастером" }
    ```
  - `401` — missing / invalid token
}
